1.4 Upgrading from version 1
============================

Version 2 replaced lsp-mode with Eglot.  If you are not ready for that,
version ‘1.1.2’ is tagged and continues to work.

   • lsp-mode, ‘dash’ and ‘compat’ are no longer dependencies; ‘eri’ and
     Eglot are.  Any lsp-mode configuration for Lean can be removed.
   • Diagnostics are reported through Flymake rather than Flycheck,
     since that is what Eglot drives.
   • The ‘lean4-keybinding-*’ options are gone.  Keys now live in
     ‘lean4-mode-map’ and are rebound the ordinary way: ‘(keymap-set
     lean4-mode-map "C-c C-i" #'lean4-toggle-info)’.
   • ‘lean4-mode-hook’ is now an ordinary mode hook.  Whether the server
     starts automatically is controlled by ‘lean4-auto-start-server’,
     which defaults to ‘t’.
   • ‘lean4-extra-arguments’ is now ‘lean4-server-arguments’; the old
     name still works.
   • Lean 3 autodetection is gone, along with ‘lean4-autodetect-lean3’.
     It ran ‘lean -v’ every time a ‘.lean’ file was opened.  Lean 3
     users should use Lean3-Mode
     (https://github.com/leanprover/lean3-mode).


